# block:journals so its previous sibling IS the de-inlined day page. If a future change
# makes this case green, FIRST confirm gen-1 still lands under block:journals — a green
# here is only meaningful if that still holds.
{"name": "indent-onto-deinlined-sibling-page-vetoes-writeback", "description": "Pre-existing keystone red, reproduced 2026-08-02 in 3 transitions: Indent(block:gen-1) re-parents a plain block onto its previous sibling, the seeded de-inlined daily journal page block:61133fe7 (2026-01-15), which lives in its OWN org file. The store performs the move correctly (the SQL render of Journals.org rightly omits gen-1), but veto_ungrounded_removals refuses that write with UNGROUNDED WRITE-BACK REMOVAL and quarantines Journals.org, so the stale on-disk copy survives. Root cause: writeback_sibling_grounding (file_sync_controller.rs:4897) resolves doc_id_to_path(block.id), which is Ok(None) for a NON-page block (name_chain returns an empty chain, sync_ports.rs:206-220), so the destination file is never read and a legitimate cross-file move is misread as data loss. Fires inv-blocks-match-ref/org (10 SUT blocks vs 9 ref, gen-1 under BOTH block:journals and block:61133fe7), inv-org-render-fixed-point (render != disk persisted 5s) and inv-no-observed-errors. INTERMITTENT on the unfixed tree — 4 RED / 4 GREEN in 8 serial runs (2026-08-03), because the veto only happens when the queued Upsert for gen-1 (which still carries the PRE-move parent) is rendered after the Indent has landed in the store. Judge any change to the write-back grounding over ~20 runs; a single green proves nothing here.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer"]}}, "transitions": [{"NavigateFocus": {"region": "main", "block_id": "block:journals"}}, {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "s", "id": "block:gen-1"}}, {"Indent": {"block_id": "block:gen-1"}}]}

